.SH COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS
.sp
\fBscconfig [options]\fP
.SS Generic
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message.
.UNINDENT
.SS Verbosity
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Execute in debug mode.
Equivalent to \-\-verbosity=4 \-\-console=1 .
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show version information.
.UNINDENT
.SS Options
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-module arg
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Name of module for which to open the configuration at startup given by
the module name, e.g. scautopick. Requires \-\-panel and is supported by
the Modules and Bindings panels. In the Bindings panel all profiles of
the module are shown and, when used with \-\-station, the parameters for
that station also show.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-panel arg
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Panel to open at startup given by its number, e.g. 2, or its name, e.g.
Modules. The number corresponds to the panel shortcut key.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-parameter arg
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Name of parameter or parameter section to navigate to at startup
given by its full name, e.g., connection.server or database.
Requires \-\-panel and \-module for Modules panel or \-\-panel, \-\-module
and \-\-station for Bindings panel.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-station arg
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Station to show the bindings of at startup given as NET.STA, e.g.
GE.APE. Requires \-\-panel and is supported by the Bindings panel. If
combined with \-\-module, the parameters of the module binding at that
station also show.
.UNINDENT
